# Miro-to-Failure-Model Tool Rules

## Subproject Context
This tool converts Miro Backcasting Maps into the repository's curated Failure
Model Markdown.

## Key Specifications
- Node format: `../../schemas/failure-model/node-spec.md`
- Board rules: `../../schemas/failure-model/miro-board-rules.md`
- Mapping rules: `../../schemas/failure-model/miro-mapping-spec.md`
- Product direction: `../../docs/traceability/registry.md`

## Technical Stack (Target)
- Python 3.11+
- `python-frontmatter` for Markdown parsing
- Miro REST API

## Implementation Guidelines
- Prefer plain files + conventions over database
- Preserve existing node IDs when updating; generate new IDs only for new nodes
- Treat canonical schemas and retrieval policy as external contracts.
- Do not add MCP or RAG without a new repository traceability decision.
